    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a clear strategic emphasis on volume and opportunistic matchups. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) stands as the primary anchor of our lineup; his leadoff role combined with a favorable 4.39 xERA matchup against Gusto provides elite scoring potential, even after accounting for the moderate drag from the catcher's control over the run game. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** (73.11) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (70.30) are essential core starts. **Kazuma Okamoto** benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Gibson, whose 5.35 xERA is the most exploitable pitching profile on our radar today, allowing for significant upside in the cleanup spot. \n\nPlatoon advantages and park factors are driving the middle tier of our roster. **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (69.90) and **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) are both positioned to capitalize on high-scoring environments, with **Lars Nootbaar** seeing a notable 14% lift from park factors alone. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** remains a locked-in start (63.54) despite the threat posed by Cole; his high-leverage order spot (#3) and dynamic platoon advantage provide enough buffer to weather the difficulty of the opposing arm. The closest call on the bench was **Carson Benge** (51.63), who offered a solid floor against Bradford but ultimately lost out due to a negative platoon split (L/L) and a lower ceiling compared to the primary utility options. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of the league\u2019s late-season landscape. While **Trea Turner** (49.88) holds a marginal score due to a daunting matchup against Henderson\u2014an elite arm with a 2.97 xERA\u2014his position in the #2 hole necessitates his inclusion to maintain our SB production, our scarcest category. We continue to monitor the status of **Colt Keith**, who remains on the IL, while **Hector Rodriguez** is confirmed out of the lineup. As we move into the evening, ensure **Trea Turner** and **Caleb Durbin** are monitored closely; their value is highly sensitive to opposing catchers, and any late-breaking weather shifts in the outdoor venues could further suppress their projected efficiency.",
